Description: Provides the header files of Google 'Highway'
    <https://github.com/google/highway>, a 'C++' library for portable 'SIMD'
    (single instruction, multiple data) programming, so that other packages
    can use it through 'LinkingTo'. A kernel is written once and compiled for
    several instruction sets, such as 'SSE2', 'SSE4', 'AVX2' and 'AVX-512' on
    'x86-64' and 'NEON' and 'SVE' on 'ARM64', and the best one supported by the
    running processor is chosen at run time, so binary packages need no
    processor-specific compiler flags. Also provides a single-file
    implementation of the dispatch runtime, error handling that never
    terminates the R session, guards that turn 'C++' exceptions into R errors
    or status codes at '.Call' and 'C' interfaces, and use_highway() to set up
    a package.
